---
import AuthShell from "~/components/AuthShell.astro";
---

<AuthShell
  title="Terms | LostLink"
  heading="Terms &amp; Conditions"
  subheading="Rules for using LostLink."
  description="Terms and conditions for the DLSAU lost and found system."
>
  <div class="mt-8 space-y-7 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-sage-700">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-forest-900">Who can use LostLink</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        DLSAU students, faculty, and staff with a @dlsau.edu.ph email account. One
        account per person. Accounts used for abuse may be disabled by the
        administration.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-forest-900">Report truthfully</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Report only real lost or found items. Do not submit false reports or claims.
        False claims may be denied by the security office and referred to the
        administration.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-forest-900">How claiming works</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li>Submitting a claim does not guarantee an item is released to you.</li>
        <li>
          The security office compares your proof with the physical item. Found items
          are held at the security office only.
        </li>
        <li>
          Verified claimants pick up the item in person at the security office with
          their claim reference code and DLSAU ID.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-forest-900">Your reports</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        You can edit or delete your own report only while it is pending. Approved
        reports are locked and appear as public listings without your contact details.
        Rejected reports show the reason; you can edit and resubmit them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-forest-900">Admin decisions</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Security office admins approve or reject reports and verify or deny claims.
        Decisions about physical item verification are final at the security office.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-forest-900">About this service</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        LostLink matches reports online. The physical safekeeping and handover of items
        is done by the security office. For questions about these terms, visit the
        security office.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</AuthShell>
